S141 LRC14 REGULAR-SOLID / EUCLIDEAN-TILING RECURSION CARRIER
==============================================================================
[1] Assumption challenge / quotient declaration
  considered vertices:
    regular maps {p,q}, tiling vertex figures, Euclidean recursion
    indices, Platonic/Archimedean configurations, prism/antiprism
    annuli, Johnson defect packets, q=3 unital points, C27 shells, and
    proof obligations.
  chosen predicate:
    normalized angle defect kappa = 1 - sum interior_angle/(2*pi),
    plus labelled self/dual recursion indices.
  quotient preserves:
    local curvature/defect, duality type, norm/self-recursion label,
    finite-atlas status, and whether a carrier reaches the LRC 1/14
    defect scale.
  quotient destroys:
    exact LRC time geometry, exact denominator witnesses, and pair
    incidence unless the q=3 unital layer is separately attached.
  challenged assumption:
    Solids and tilings should not be treated as one scalar analogy.
    The audit splits them into curvature walls, norm recursions, annular
    14/28 carriers, and finite Johnson residual packets.

[2] Regular map curvature boundary
  rule:
    (p-2)(q-2)<4 spherical; =4 Euclidean; >4 hyperbolic.
  Platonic finite maps:
    tetrahedron  {3,3} kind=spherical  dual=self             V,E,F=(4, 6, 4) kappa=1/2
    cube         {4,3} kind=spherical  dual=octahedron       V,E,F=(8, 12, 6) kappa=1/4
    octahedron   {3,4} kind=spherical  dual=cube             V,E,F=(6, 12, 8) kappa=1/3
    dodecahedron {5,3} kind=spherical  dual=icosahedron      V,E,F=(20, 30, 12) kappa=1/10
    icosahedron  {3,5} kind=spherical  dual=dodecahedron     V,E,F=(12, 30, 20) kappa=1/6
  regular Euclidean tilings:
    triangular tiling  {3,6} kind=Euclidean  dual=hexagonal tiling   kappa=0
    square tiling      {4,4} kind=Euclidean  dual=self               kappa=0
    hexagonal tiling   {6,3} kind=Euclidean  dual=triangular tiling  kappa=0
  readout:
    Platonic solids are positive-curvature finite skeletons.  The plane
    regular tilings are the zero-curvature recursion wall, not the same
    scalar object.

